<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27754" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mallo</span></b> , ōnis,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαλλός</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The stem</i> of onions (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mallonem caeparum, id est calamos siccos, unde
					fasces dependent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. Vet. 2, 60</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1, 63</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A kind of tumor on the knees</i> in animals,
					<i><span class="en">Veg. Vet. 2, 48, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
